**Rationale for the `LOCATE` node** (the design's single most consequential component).
The goal objective names `reviews/tasks/B0.N_review.md` as the corpus. But A8's claim is
about the artifact set PAEOS produces across **L06, L08, L11, the decision graph, and the
scar graph** (SAEOS-1 §6.1b lists exactly which node type comes from which stage). A review
document is one artifact class, most plausibly the L10/L14 verdict. Extracting from review
documents *alone* would score `Constraint` (L11), `Component` (L08) and `TradeOff` (L06) as
absent for a reason that has nothing to do with prose being unstructured — producing a
**false NO-GO** that would kill a viable S1.

`LOCATE` therefore treats the review document as the **entry point and index**, and resolves
outward to whatever else the goal sealed. Slots unreachable after a logged locate attempt
are scored `absent-out-of-corpus` (§3.3), which counts as loss but is *attributed* separately
so the verdict can distinguish *"PAEOS's prose is too unstructured"* (fatal to Ω1) from
*"the bundle needs a multi-artifact assembler"* (an S1 work item, not a falsification).

**No orphan:** every node above has an inbound and outbound edge; `PR` is deliberately
inbound-only to `EXTRACT`/`SCORE`/`VERDICT` and has no inbound edge — it is frozen input.

