stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> PRE_REGISTER
    PRE_REGISTER --> LOCATE: §3 inventory + §3.4 exclusions + §5.1 rule frozen
    LOCATE --> EXTRACT: artifact set resolved per goal (found/not-found logged)
    LOCATE --> DIVERSITY_ADD: all of G1-G3 are pure scaffolding (§7.1)
    DIVERSITY_ADD --> LOCATE: add G4
    EXTRACT --> SECOND_PASS: G1,G2 done; G3 first pass frozen
    SECOND_PASS --> AGREEMENT: G3 second pass frozen (blind)
    AGREEMENT --> SCORE: agreement_rate computed
    SCORE --> AGGREGATE: D, N computed (§4)
    AGGREGATE --> VERDICT: apply frozen §5.1 rule
    VERDICT --> EMIT: GO or NO-GO
    EMIT --> [*]: §6.1 artifact + §6.2 self-test

    AGGREGATE --> BLOCKED: D = 0 (§6.3)
    BLOCKED --> [*]: gate reported FAILED, no fabricated ratio

    EXTRACT --> VOID: pre-registration amended after EXTRACT began
    SECOND_PASS --> VOID: second extractor saw the first ledger
    VOID --> [*]: probe discarded, re-run from PRE_REGISTER

    note right of VOID
      The falsifiability guard. A probe whose
      threshold or rubric moved after seeing
      data proves nothing about A8 and must
      not be reported as if it did.
    end note
```

Every state has an entry and an exit; `VOID` and `BLOCKED` are terminal by design, and both
route to a re-run rather than to a reported verdict.

