## 10. Perspectives covered (multi-perspective critique input, L09)

- **Correctness.** The verdict is a pure function of the frozen §5.1 rule over the field
  ledger; §4's arithmetic is total over `D > 0` and the `D = 0` branch is specified (§6.3).
  Every score maps to exactly one weight, and every slot to exactly one class (§3.2) — the
  partition is disjoint and exhaustive. ✔
- **Falsifiability (K6, Δ3).** The probe can fail, and four distinct failure modes are named
  in advance with distinct consequences (§5.4). Pre-registration + the `VOID` transitions
  (§8) close the retrofit-the-threshold hole that makes most spikes unfalsifiable. ✔
- **Adversarial / anti-rigging.** Three independent rigging vectors are closed: denominator
  laundering (§3.4), single-extractor confirmation bias (§5.3), and average-hides-spine
  (C2/C3 as hard gates). The `0.00` fabrication incentive is named and forbidden (§6.3). ✔
- **Non-authority (FPL-3).** The probe reads sealed artifacts and writes one spike document.
  It gates nothing, promotes nothing, and mints no evidence. Its findings are **proposals**
  routed to ratification (§7.3), never edits to SAEOS-1 — CER-5, and the same restraint
  SAEOS-1 §9 A6 exercises on the dual-constitution problem. ✔
- **Separation of powers / scope discipline.** DESIGN writes only `design/`; the probe
  artifact, the corpus read, and the verdict all belong to the downstream stage (§0). This
  document deliberately withholds any prediction of the outcome. ✔
- **Cost.** Bounded by construction: 3 goals (+1 conditional), 7 node types, ~3+n slots per
  node instance, one double pass. No tooling to build; nothing here presumes a parser exists
  — the spike is *why* we do not yet build one. ✔
- **Sequencing.** SAEOS-1 §8 makes S1+S2 *"the whole bet"* and §9 makes A8 load-bearing for
  the entire delivery path. Running this before S1 implementation is the cheapest possible
  falsification point; every later one costs more (Δ8's lesson — serializing risk to the end
  guarantees maximum sunk cost before first falsification). ✔
- **What a GO does *not* license.** Feasibility of *hand* extraction, on 3–4 B0 goals only.
  Not automatability, not generalization to mature goals, not §8 S1's `lossless`. Stated in
  the artifact so a GO cannot be over-read downstream (§7.2). ✔

